{"id":225861550014655,"type":"album","name":"Twitch","artist":"Ministry","year":1986,"weight":24,"info":{"cover":"https://dn710608.ca.archive.org/0/items/mbid-13a66df4-ce5c-4e8e-9ba1-8766decf5676/mbid-13a66df4-ce5c-4e8e-9ba1-8766decf5676-28680783980.jpg","kind":"Album","tracks":9,"country":"US","scaruffi":7.0,"yt":"sVdPrET44P4","links":{"spotify":"https://open.spotify.com/album/1CEBvP4PPZatx4SH3vTbm6","youtube":"https://music.youtube.com/playlist?list=OLAK5uy_nzR--bhxZRGvmNWSGzRIxZSZitAPaI5_g","rateyourmusic":"https://rateyourmusic.com/release/album/ministry/twitch"},"desc":"Twitch is the second studio album by industrial metal band Ministry, released in 1986. The album stepped away from the synthpop-oriented form of their previous debut album With Sympathy (1983) and moved toward a darker, more aggressive sound in the form of EBM. Released by Sire Records, Jourgensen was granted more artistic control over the production than under Arista/BMG. Twitch was re-released in 1990 with two additional tracks. Twitched, an unauthorized 2003 release by Radioactive Records, is a remastered version of Twitch, featuring the track listing that the band is said to have intended it to have before the intervention ."},"artist_ref":{"id":8164776207386,"name":"Ministry","info":{"img":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Hellfest2017Ministry_14.jpg?width=500"}},"labels":[],"genres":[{"id":274994627985231,"type":"genre","name":"Industrial","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":604,"yt":null,"src":"musthear"},{"id":242119982771334,"type":"genre","name":"Electro","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":345,"yt":null,"src":"musthear"},{"id":97399718380223,"type":"genre","name":"dance-rock","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":39,"yt":null,"src":"musthear"},{"id":107889004937350,"type":"genre","name":"EBM","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":237,"yt":null,"src":"rym"},{"id":23184402430853,"type":"genre","name":"Electro-Industrial","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":213,"yt":null,"src":